  "notes": "I = inv + sum_{p<pos1}(m-2t+1) is the inversion count of the token order starting at token 1 (zeros skipped; checked against inv=28). excess = sum((p-pos1) mod n) - m(m-1)/2. e=I+excess is 0 iff csorted, L/R-invariant, and an improving X (t>1 with zero or larger token immediately CCW; token 1 fixed) drops it by exactly 1. k is circular distance to the nearest such left cell, so one of L,R drops k by 1, and after X the new k is at most floor(n/2). Thus phi=(floor(n/2)+1)*e+k descends; csorted uses rot_dist. e is O(m^2+mr) rather than the weighted anchor sum, so the same multiplier yields a much smaller potential."
